---
import PublishedLayout from '../components/layout/PublishedLayout.astro';
import { sources } from '../data/sources';

const sourceCount = sources.length;
---

<PublishedLayout pageIntentId="pi-feature-about">
  <section class="page-heading wrapper">
    <p class="eyebrow">About Fitwise</p>
    <h1>Dimension-based fit tools, with assumptions made visible</h1>
    <p>
      Fitwise helps people compare measured objects with rooms, work surfaces and openings before
      they buy, arrange or move items. Tools accept metric and imperial measurements; internal
      geometry uses millimetres.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrapper section" aria-labelledby="editorial-approach">
    <h2 id="editorial-approach">How the information is handled</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Product dimensions are tied to a named model and source where those measurements are
        available.
      </li>
      <li>
        Derived geometry is identified as calculated, and display-panel estimates are not presented
        as full device dimensions.
      </li>
      <li>
        User-entered measurements and clearance preferences are separate from sourced product facts.
      </li>
      <li>
        Results are dimensional screening estimates, not delivery guarantees, building-code
        interpretations, safety reviews or ergonomic recommendations.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <a href="/methodology/">Read the calculation methodology</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrapper section" aria-labelledby="data-sources">
    <h2 id="data-sources">Data sources</h2>
    <p>
      The registry currently contains {sourceCount} references. Source confidence is editorial
      metadata about the record, not a statistical confidence interval. Product-specific dimensions
      can vary by model, configuration, market and revision; verify the exact model before relying
      on a measurement.
    </p>
    <div class="source-list">
      {sources.map((source) => (
        <article class="source-card" id={`source-${source.id}`}>
          <h3>{source.url ? <a href={source.url}>{source.title}</a> : source.title}</h3>
          <dl>
            <div>
              <dt>Publisher</dt>
              <dd>{source.publisher}</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Accessed</dt>
              <dd>
                <time datetime={source.accessedOn}>{source.accessedOn}</time>
              </dd>
            </div>
            {source.geography && (
              <div>
                <dt>Geography</dt>
                <dd>{source.geography}</dd>
              </div>
            )}
            {source.standard && (
              <div>
                <dt>Standard</dt>
                <dd>{source.standard}</dd>
              </div>
            )}
            <div>
              <dt>Record confidence</dt>
              <dd>{source.confidence}</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
          {source.notes && <p>{source.notes}</p>}
          {source.id === 'src-fitwise-internal-convention' && (
            <p>
              <a href="/methodology/reference-conventions/">
                Public reference-size and clearance conventions
              </a>
            </p>
          )}
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrapper section" id="corrections" aria-labelledby="corrections-heading">
    <h2 id="corrections-heading">Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      A verified source change should update the associated source record and measurements; a
      calculation defect should update the shared geometry and gain a regression test. Where product
      dimensions differ, the current manufacturer documentation for the exact model takes precedence
      over a representative Fitwise example. Assumptions that are not directly sourced should remain
      labeled as assumptions.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="https://github.com/nikatsam/Website_fitwise/issues/new?template=correction.yml">
        Report a measurement or calculation correction on GitHub
      </a>
      . Include the page URL, exact model, current source or manual and a reproducible description.
      Do not include private addresses or personal information. Reports are public issues; no
      response-time commitment is implied.
    </p>
  </section>
</PublishedLayout>

<style>
  .page-heading {
    padding-block: var(--space-7) var(--space-3);
  }

  .page-heading h1 {
    max-width: 22ch;
    margin-block: var(--space-1) var(--space-3);
    font-size: var(--fs-3xl);
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
  }

  .page-heading > p:last-child,
  .section > p {
    max-width: 76ch;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-accent-1);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .section {
    padding-block: var(--space-6);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .source-list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 22rem), 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-3);
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }

  .source-card {
    min-width: 0;
    padding: var(--space-4);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    background: var(--color-surface-raised);
  }

  .source-card h3 {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .source-card h3 a {
    color: inherit;
  }

  .source-card dl {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  }

  .source-card dl div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(6.5rem, 0.4fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }

  .source-card dt {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .source-card dd {
    min-width: 0;
    margin: 0;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .source-card > p {
    margin: var(--space-3) 0 0;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
</style>
